  "articleBody": "Bringing down trim, doors, and custom shelving to turn a lower level into comfortable living space takes extra care. Unlike upstairs rooms, basements face slab moisture and foundation shifts that demand specific carpentry choices.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\n- Moisture protection: Untreated wood should never contact bare concrete slabs directly. Look for pressure-treated bottom plates or capillary breaks to prevent rot and warping.\n- Finished floor height: Confirm exact flooring thickness before hanging interior doors or trimming baseboards, or you will end up trimming doors twice.\n- Utility clearances: Built-in cabinets, shelving, and wall paneling must maintain clean access points to electrical panels, shutoff valves, and cleanouts.\n- Framing stability: Uneven basement concrete walls require careful shimming and scribing so casings and baseboards sit flat without visible gaps.\n\nA qualified professional becomes important when dealing with basement staircases, tight tolerances around mechanicals, or custom built-in units that need precise anchoring. Abraham Becerra and the team at HH Remodeling LLC handle basement finish carpentry throughout the Denver metro area, taking care of framing, doors, and trim with hands-on oversight. Call 303-505-0866 to review your basement plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
